Z||000000||Neal||06-01-2001||02:53 PM||||err 2.8 pan on a 3.4<P>Ok ive been through the search, archives, and many wbsites but cant find my answer.<P>I have an 87 and a 3.4 out of a camaro is gonna go in. Can i use my 87 pan on the block?<P>The best i could find is that it is possible to use the 86 pan and timing cover but the pan needed to be modified.  Modified how?<P>Im only having this issue because i got a GREAT deal on the 3.4 block crank and rods, but no oil pan.<P>Also if need be i have an 86 compleate engine that i can use for oil pan and timing cover.<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||06-01-2001||04:31 PM||||yes you can but the metal piece inside the pan that surrounds the oil pump neck needs to be trimmed to accommodate the oil pump on the 3.4.........<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                  </A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||06-01-2001||04:32 PM||||The '87 pan and front cover will bolt up to the 3.4.  You will need the '87 Fiero front cover as it is diff for the Fiero vs other 60 degree V6s.  I'm not sure if the pans are the same exact part #, but the Fiero pan will bolt on and should be used.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||06-01-2001||05:21 PM||||Thanks<BR>Now for another question, i have both the 86 and 87 design.  Whisch is better?||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||06-01-2001||06:36 PM||||the '87, it is a year newer.......... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||06-02-2001||01:17 AM||||I don't recall if the design change happened in '86 or '87.  Anyway, use the later one as the 1 piece oil pan seals much better when your engine gets a few miles on it.  Of course the oil pan gasket is over 3 times the $$...||||reg||1
